<title>USA: Armstrong World Q3 shr rises despite charge.</title>
<headline>Armstrong World Q3 shr rises despite charge.</headline>
<dateline>LANCASTER, Pa. 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.86		    $0.40</p>
<p> Net			 35,800		   19,400</p>
<p> Sales		    563,400		  611,800</p>
<p>	  9  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $2.34		    $2.33</p>
<p> Net			102,700		  106,500</p>
<p> Sales		  1,627,800		1,767,400</p>
<p>(All data above 000s)  </p>
<p>NOTE - 1996 Q3 net EPS includes an after-tax charge of $22 million, or $0.53 per share, for discoloration of a limited portion of its residential inlaid color sheet flooring product lines and $8.4 million, or $0.20 per share, for its share of an extraordinary loss from Dal-Tile International Inc's refinancing of outstanding debt.</p>
<p>Excluding those charges, the company posted Q3 earnings of $66.2 million, or $1.59 per share, compared to $56.3 million, or $1.14 per share, in the same period in 1995.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
